# Handoff scratch — the cycle's working surface, deleted when the cycle ends.
#
# All three files are transient and none of them is a record. The plan is
# discarded; the findings mailbox is a triage scratchpad, deleted once every
# finding's disposition is written into the body of the commit that answers it
# (behavioral rule 20, `adversarial-review` step 9). Git history is already
# tracked, dated, and immutable, so the dispositions need no file of their own —
# `git log --grep="adversary round"` reads them back. Do not add a tracked
# review report here; that is `/project:review`'s artifact, not this one's.
#
# Note these globs match only names ending exactly in `-plan.md` / `-findings.md` /
# `-handoff.md`;
# a suffixed variant (`auth-plan-v2.md`) is NOT ignored and will surface as
# untracked, failing the clean-tree gate at the end of the cycle. One file per
# slug, no suffixes.
#
# The third file is the handoff brief (`llm-handoff` skill): a prompt for an
# external agent, not repo content. That agent deletes it when its cycle ends.
.harness/handoff/*-plan.md
.harness/handoff/*-findings.md
.harness/handoff/*-handoff.md

# Obsidian per-user vault config (users open the vault themselves)
docs/.obsidian/
